Buran embedded runtime
======================

Buran source and desktop-exit helper provenance:
https://github.com/intercontinentalmassacre/Buran
Base revision 93ac7b3e8f3540960308fdce048a6f39a995ac52

The desktop-exit PE helpers shipped in src/main/assets are built from
native/windows/desktop-exit.c and desktop-exit-kernel32.def. Their SHA-256 hashes:
  buran-desktop-exit.exe     b68f2d493e9b4257884031bf922c6e536814007885f1b17978887f21923b0e18
  buran-desktop-exit-x86.exe 0077a94d316ff9065258b42a1def74373f89ce46b1764d7fa75ce26c4b3e9a58

Gameplay's performance HUD appears under org.buran.runtime.hud. Source
attribution is in the adapted Kotlin files and the GNU GPL version 3 text is
bundled in assets/notices/gameplay-performance-hud-gpl-3.0.txt.

Third-party runtime payloads are staged by prepare-runtime.sh. The Box package
inventory and SHA-256 values are in box/packages.txt. The renderer and Wine
release URLs and digests are in their staging scripts. The APK includes
third-party notices under assets/notices, and the guest archives retain the
notices of their bundled packages.

Prebuilt Gameplay ports
-----------------------

The Buran variants of the Steam bootstrap, redirect and KGSL ports are
packaged under prebuilt/gameplay-ports. The Steam bootstrap runs as an
Android child executable. The redirect and KGSL shims run in the runtime
or guest subprocesses that load them. The source and build script for
these binaries are maintained separately in Gameplay's private native
component repository. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in the Gameplay repository
for the corresponding upstream components and their notices.
